To conduct a structured brainstorming session for identifying product ideas, user needs, and business objectives.

Requirements
Laptop/Desktop
Internet Connection
Google Docs / MS Word
Team Members (Optional)
Step 1: Define the Problem Statement

Open MS Word or Google Docs.

Write a problem statement.

Example:

Students need an easy online platform to manage college assignments.

This becomes the discussion topic.

Step 2: Identify Target Users

Write who will use the product.

Example:

User Type	Need
Students	Upload assignments
Faculty	Check submissions
Admin	Manage records
Step 3: Create Brainstorming Document

Create headings:

1. Problem
2. Ideas
3. Features
4. Challenges
5. Final Solution
Step 4: Conduct Idea Generation Session

Ask team members to suggest ideas.

Example ideas:

Mobile App
Notification System
Cloud Storage
Login System
Deadline Reminder

Write all ideas in document.

Step 5: Categorize Ideas

Separate ideas into categories.

Example:

Category	Ideas
Functional	Assignment Upload
Security	User Login
Communication	Notifications
Step 6: Prioritize Important Features

Select most useful features.

Example:

Priority	Feature
High	Assignment Upload
High	Notifications
Medium	Dark Mode
Step 7: Analyze Feasibility

Check whether features are:

Easy to implement
Cost effective
Useful to users

Example:

Cloud storage is feasible because Oracle Cloud provides storage services.
Step 8: Create Final Solution Plan

Write final product summary.

Example:

Develop a cloud-based assignment management system with notifications and secure login.
Step 9: Prepare Brainstorming Report

Include:

Problem Statement
Team Ideas
Selected Features
Final Solution

Save document as:

Brainstorming_Report.docx
Step 10: Review and Discuss

Discuss:

Advantages
Limitations
Future improvements

Finalize the report.

Implementation & Result

Successfully:

Identified user requirements
Generated product ideas
Prioritized features
Prepared final solution document

Structured brainstorming session conducted successfully.
